  "description": "1) A brick wall fronting a steel box with a 'green' roof. The brick wall serves as the boundary wall between the pavement and the front yard. The box serves as outdoor storage and supports a steel planter. Approx dimensions: W 2800mm x D 800-900mm x H 1450mm (wall height of 1250mm + 200mm planter)\nGroundworks include a new concrete slab, to which the box will be secured and bricks laid.\nThe width of the new wall approximately replaces the same width of the existing wall, so the gate/entryway to the property will be unchanged.\n2) A brick and timber wheelie bin housing, with a 'green' roof. Two lateral brick walls and a central steel upright to support a planter similar to part 1. The highway facing wall is made up of a removeable steel frame, braced with timber panels.",
